        "title": "Expense Deductions - How Much Can You Save (Part 2)",
        "content": "TAXABLE INCOME: Rs.10,00,000 - Rs.2,26,100 = Rs.7,73,900\n\nNow, Rahul has a choice:\nOption A: Claim actual expenses (Rs.2,26,100 deduction)\nOption B: Use 44ADA (50% of Rs.10L = Rs.5,00,000 deduction)\n\n44ADA gives more deduction (Rs.5,00,000 > Rs.2,26,100)\nSo Rahul should use 44ADA!\n\nTaxable under 44ADA: Rs.5,00,000\nTax (New Regime): Rs.10,000 (approx)\nTax (Old Regime with 80C etc.): Rs.7,500 (approx)\n\nRahul saves Rs.2,500 by using Old Regime + 44ADA!\n```\n\n**Key Learning:** Always compare actual expenses vs 44ADA. Whichever gives more deduction, use that!\n\n### Deep Dive: Depreciation Rules for Freelancers\n\nUnderstanding depreciation is important because you cannot claim the entire cost of expensive equipment in one year - the government says you must account for wear and tear.\n\n**Depreciation Rates (Income Tax Act):**\n\n| Asset | Depreciation Rate | Useful Life | Method |\n|-------|-------------------|-------------|--------|\n| Computers/Laptops | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Software | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Phones/Tablets | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Cameras | 40% | 3 years | WDV |\n| Furniture | 10% | 10 years | WDV |\n| Office Equipment | 15% | 7 years | WDV |\n| Vehicles | 15% | 7 years | WDV |\n\n**WDV = Written Down Value** - meaning depreciation is applied on the remaining value each year.\n\n**Depreciation Calculation Example:**\n\n```\nSha bought a camera for Rs.80,000 in 2024\n\nYear 1 (2024-25):\nOpening Value: Rs.80,000\nDepreciation: 40% of Rs.80,000 = Rs.32,000\nClosing Value: Rs.48,000\n\nYear 2 (2025-26):\nOpening Value: Rs.48,000\nDepreciation: 40% of Rs.48,000 = Rs.19,200\nClosing Value: Rs.28,800\n\nYear 3 (2026-27):\nOpening Value: Rs.28,800\nDepreciation: 40% of Rs.28,800 = Rs.11,520\nClosing Value: Rs.17,280\n\nTotal Depreciation Claimed: Rs.32,000 + Rs.19,200 + Rs.11,520 = Rs.62,720\n```\n\n**Important Points:**\n1. Proof of asset is needed (invoice, bank statement)\n2. Calculate business usage percentage\n3. If 50% personal + 50% business, claim only 50% depreciation",
