        "title": "Old Regime vs New Regime - Which is Best for Freelancers",
        "content": "In Module 10 we covered basic comparison. Now let us do a detailed analysis for freelancers.\n\n### Detailed Comparison for Freelancer Income Slabs\n\n| Income Level | Old Regime Tax | New Regime Tax | Better Regime | Savings |\n|-------------|---------------|----------------|---------------|---------|\n| Rs.3,00,000 | Rs.0 (87A rebate) | Rs.0 (87A rebate) | Both Same | Rs.0 |\n| Rs.5,00,000 | Rs.12,500 | Rs.10,000 | New Regime | Rs.2,500 |\n| Rs.6,00,000 | Rs.22,500 | Rs.22,500 | Both Same | Rs.0 |\n| Rs.8,00,000 | Rs.62,500 | Rs.35,000 | New Regime | Rs.27,500 |\n| Rs.10,00,000 | Rs.1,12,500 | Rs.60,000 | New Regime | Rs.52,500 |\n| Rs.12,00,000 | Rs.1,62,500 | Rs.90,000 | New Regime | Rs.72,500 |\n| Rs.15,00,000 | Rs.2,62,500 | Rs.1,50,000 | New Regime | Rs.1,12,500 |\n| Rs.20,00,000 | Rs.4,12,500 | Rs.3,00,000 | New Regime | Rs.1,12,500 |\n\n**Note:** These calculations assume NO deductions under Old Regime. If you have deductions, Old Regime might be better!\n\n### When Old Regime is Better\n\nOld Regime is better when:\n1. **You have many deductions** (80C, 80D, 80CCD etc.)\n2. **Income is below Rs.10 lakh** and deductions are Rs.2-3 lakh\n3. **You have home loan interest** (Section 24)\n4. **You pay rent** (HRA exemption)\n5. **You have education loan** (Section 80E)\n\n**Priya's Old Regime Calculation:**\n```\nPriya's Income: Rs.8,00,000\n\nDeductions:\nSection 80C (ELSS): Rs.1,50,000\nSection 80D (Health Insurance): Rs.25,000\nSection 80CCD(1B) (NPS): Rs.50,000\nSection 24 (Home Loan Interest): Rs.2,00,000\nTotal Deductions: Rs.4,25,000\n\nOld Regime:\nTaxable Income: Rs.8,00,000 - Rs.4,25,000 = Rs.3,75,000\nTax: Rs.7,500 (5% on Rs.1,50,000)\n87A Rebate: Rs.7,500\nTax: ZERO!\n\nNew Regime:\nTaxable Income: Rs.8,00,000 - Rs.50,000 = Rs.7,50,000\nTax: Rs.32,500\n87A Rebate: Not applicable (income above Rs.7L)\nTax: Rs.32,500\n\nOLD REGIME SAVES: Rs.32,500!\n```\n\n### When New Regime is Better\n\nNew Regime is better when:\n1. **Few deductions** (below Rs.1.5 lakh)\n2. **Income above Rs.7 lakh** (no 87A rebate)\n3. **No home loan or HRA**\n4. **Simple tax filing** wanted",
