        "title": "Retirement Planning for Freelancers - Pension Without a Company",
        "content": "Retirement planning is crucial for freelancers because no company gives EPF. You have to plan yourself!\n\n### Why Freelancers Need to Plan Retirement\n\n| Salaried Person | Freelancer |\n|-----------------|------------|\n| Company contributes to EPF | No EPF |\n| Fixed monthly income | Irregular income |\n| Pension after retirement | No pension |\n| Gratuity after 5 years | No gratuity |\n| Health insurance by company | Self-insured |\n\n**Reality Check:** If you retire at 60 from 25, you need to save for **35 years of expenses!**\n\n### Options Available\n\n#### 1. NPS (National Pension System)\n\nNPS is a government retirement scheme - very powerful!\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Extra Rs.50,000 tax deduction under Section 80CCD(1B)\n- Market-linked returns (10-12% average)\n- Low cost (0.01% annual charges)\n- Tax-free maturity (with conditions)\n\n**NPS Returns Comparison:**\n\n| Fund Manager | 5-Year Return | 10-Year Return | Category |\n|--------------|---------------|----------------|----------|\n| SBI Pension Fund | 11.2% | 12.5% | Government |\n| LIC Pension Fund | 10.8% | 11.9% | Government |\n| HDFC Pension Fund | 12.1% | 13.2% | Private |\n| ICICI Prudential | 11.9% | 12.8% | Private |\n\n**How to Open NPS:**\n1. Visit eNPS portal (eNPS.nsdl.com)\n2. Complete KYC (Aadhaar + PAN)\n3. Choose pension fund manager\n4. Choose allocation (Equity/Corporate/Government)\n5. Start investing (minimum Rs.1,000/year)\n\n**Amit's NPS Strategy:**\n```\nAmit (22 years) invests Rs.50,000/year in NPS\nExpected return: 12% p.a.\nInvestment period: 38 years (till age 60)\n\nFuture Value: Rs.50,000 x [(1.12)^38 - 1] / 0.12\n= Rs.50,000 x [85.9 - 1] / 0.12\n= Rs.50,000 x 707.5\n= Rs.3,53,75,000 = Rs.3.54 crore!\n\nTax saved: Rs.50,000 x 30% = Rs.15,000/year\nTotal tax saved: Rs.15,000 x 38 = Rs.5,70,000\n```\n\n#### 2. PPF (Public Provident Fund)\n\nA government guaranteed scheme - safe and steady!\n\n**PPF Features:**\n- 15-year lock-in (extendable in 5-year blocks)\n- Current interest rate: 7.1% p.a.\n- Tax deduction under Section 80C\n- Tax-free maturity\n- Minimum Rs.500/year, maximum Rs.1,50,000/year",
