        "content": "#### 3. ELSS (Equity Linked Savings Scheme)\n\nMutual funds with tax benefits - best of both worlds!\n\n**ELSS Features:**\n- Shortest lock-in: 3 years\n- Tax deduction under Section 80C\n- Potential returns: 12-15% p.a.\n- Can start with Rs.500/month SIP\n\n**ELSS vs PPF vs NPS Comparison:**\n\n| Feature | ELSS | PPF | NPS |\n|---------|------|-----|-----|\n| Lock-in | 3 years | 15 years | Till 60 |\n| Returns | 12-15% | 7.1% | 10-12% |\n| Tax Benefit | 80C (Rs.1.5L) | 80C (Rs.1.5L) | 80CCD(1B) (Rs.50K) |\n| Risk | Market risk | Zero risk | Moderate risk |\n| Best For | Growth | Safety | Retirement corpus |\n\n#### 4. Health Insurance (Non-Negotiable)\n\nFreelancers must have health insurance - no company backup!\n\n**Recommended Coverage:**\n- Minimum Rs.10 lakh sum insured\n- Family floater if married\n- Super top-up for extra protection\n- Compare on PolicyBazaar, Digit, Acko\n\n### Amit's Retirement Plan at 22\n\n```\nAMIT'S MONTHLY ALLOCATION:\n\nNPS: Rs.4,167/month (Rs.50,000/year)\nELSS SIP: Rs.4,167/month (Rs.50,000/year)\nPPF: Rs.4,167/month (Rs.50,000/year)\nHealth Insurance: Rs.1,500/month (Rs.18,000/year)\n\nTotal Monthly: Rs.14,000\nTotal Annual: Rs.1,68,000\n\nProjected Corpus at 60:\nNPS: Rs.3.54 crore\nELSS: Rs.2.89 crore (at 12% CAGR)\nPPF: Rs.1.12 crore (at 7.1%)\n\nTotal: Rs.7.55 crore!\n```\n\n---",
